To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: alpha switched to XFree86
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=101985962711523

Hi,

I've commited the bits that make the XFree86 4.2.0 'XFree86' server
work with TGA cards on the alpha using the "wsfb" driver.

It will appear in the next X snapshot for alpha or if you track
-current and rebuild XF4 after your next update. 

The wsfb driver supports both 8 and 24bpp TGA cards. It's an
unaccelerated dumb framebuffer driver, but it gives slightly better
performances than the old Xtga server, and has most bells and whistles
of modern X servers.

Since it's a XFree86 server, you'll need an /etc/X11/XF86Config
configuration file. A default one is installed by the snaphots or by
"make install" in XF4. You don't need to edit it, except to change the
keyboard layout or mouse options, and --for now-- to explicitely
specify a default depth of 24 if you have a 24bpp TGA card. 

Also note that (unaccelerated) GLX and freetype2 are enabled now on
the alpha. There are probably some LP64 bugs remaining in these
package. Bug reports and fixes are welcome.

The Xtga server from xc-old is still there for now, in case
XFree86+wsfb causes problems, but I expect to remove it in a couple of
weeks if no major problems are reported with the new code. 

VGA graphics cards are still not supported by X on the alpha (although
a couple of drivers are built and installed, they don't work yet). But
things are progressing slowly...
