>>>>> "Peter" == Peter Rye <prye@shiraz.apana.org.au> writes:

    Peter> I'm now completing the install of the rest of the 3.1 snapshot.

I'm pleased to report that it all looks good. Thanks for the help.

    Peter> On an unrelated note, is there an obvious work around for the
    Peter> time stamp problem with some alphas using a different epoch to
    Peter> most machines? My alpha thinks it 2022 under OpenBSD. I can't
    Peter> seem to find any documentation about this anywhere. I presume
    Peter> there is an easy solution.

To follow up on my own post, in case anyone might find the same
problem. This is/was "_user error_". 

The problem stems from the use of AlphaBIOS/MILO for Linux, prior to
installing and using SRM. As a result, I was inadvertently using the wrong
options for /sbin/clock, which combined with an incorrect clock setting had
everything _appearing_ to be properly configured. OpenBSD was doing the
right thing all along. My fault, sorry.

    Peter> Thanks, Peter Rye
