On Wed, Apr 10, 2002 at 12:29:00PM -0600, Ryan Anderson wrote:
| Where the heck do you get DEC NICs these days? I can find the technical 
| specs for them on compaq's site, but I can't seem to find anyone 
| actually selling one new. Are they out of production? Is ebay my only 
| option?

There's lots of places to get DEC-alike chips. The D-Link 4-way NIC
has four 21143's on 'em. Search misc@ archives for references. You'll
find many a posting from Henning explaining why these chips are A-OK
(and why you should use dc(4) instead of de(4)). All of these *should*
work in your alpha (assuming PCI NICs here ;).

Hope that helps.

Paul 'WEiRD' de Weerd

